  "releaseNotes": "Version 4.5.0:\n              - Add opt-in, per-provider full TraceLogging schema hashing to distinguish events that reuse a name with different fields. Call enable_trace_logging_full_schema_hashing() before enabling the provider; hashing is disabled by default.\n              - Bound TraceLogging event-name reads and validate metadata lengths, including metadata within larger extended-data buffers.\n              - Fix schema-key copy assignment recursion and preserve owned event names, including assignments from borrowed names.\n              - Add user-trace provider-enable error callbacks via set_enable_provider_error_callback(). A handled failure can allow the remaining providers to be enabled.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": false,
  "summary": "Krabs ETW provides a modern C++ wrapper around the low-level ETW trace consumption functions",
